          "p": "Two of his ideas are abused more than any others (the *will to power* and the line about *no facts, only interpretations*), and both abuses come from quoting him loosely, or quoting things he never published. Both require careful custody: getting the ideas right, and flagging plainly where a famous 'Nietzsche' is not actually Nietzsche. The will to power comes first, and its cartoon (a lust to dominate other people, the philosophy of the bully) is exactly backward."
